\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A professional 
\f1\fs26 \cb3 DESIGN.md
\f0\fs24 \cb1  file is a two-layer structured specification
\f2\b0  that translates a brand's user interface rules into an open-standard format natively understood by AI coding agents. Originally open-sourced by Google Labs (via Google Stitch), it combines machine-readable 
\f0\b YAML design tokens
\f2\b0  with human-readable 
\f0\b markdown design rationale
\f2\b0  to prevent AI from generating generic "AI slop" interfaces. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\
Popular repositories like the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/VoltAgent/awesome-design-md/"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 VoltAgent/awesome-design-md GitHub repository}} provide production-ready 
\f3\fs26 \cb3 DESIGN.md
\f2\fs24 \cb1  files for top design systems like Stripe, Apple, Linear, and Notion. [5, 6]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 \strokec2 The Two-Layer Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 A valid, professional 
\f3\fs26 \cb3 DESIGN.md
\f2\fs24 \cb1  file is strictly split into two layers within the same document: [3]\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The YAML Frontmatter (Data Layer):
\f2\b0  Strict, machine-readable variables for keys like colors, border radii, and spacing.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Markdown Prose (Intent Layer):
\f2\b0  Rules, constraints, and instructions that explain 
\f4\i why
\f2\i0  these values exist and 
\f4\i how
\f2\i0  they apply. [2, 3, 5]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 \strokec2 Professional 
\f1 \cb3 DESIGN.md
\f0 \cb1  Production Template\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 To use this, drop a file named 
\f3\fs26 \cb3 DESIGN.md
\f2\fs24 \cb1  into your project's root folder. Claude Code, Cursor, or Google Stitch will automatically read it as a visual blueprint. [6, 7]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\
# ============================================================================\
# LAYER 1: MACHINE-READABLE DESIGN TOKENS (YAML Frontmatter)\
# ============================================================================\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 theme: "Modern Minimalist"\
version: "1.0.0"\
\
tokens:\
  colors:\
    primary: "#11171B"     # Core text and dominant structural elements\
    surface: "#FFFFFF"     # Primary page background\
    muted: "#8C9A9E"       # Low-contrast secondary text and subtle borders\
    accent: "#44545B"      # Interaction states, highlights, and primary CTAs\
    error: "#D9383A"       # System destructive actions or alerts\
  \
  typography:\
    sans: "Inter, system-ui, sans-serif"\
    mono: "JetBrains Mono, monospace"\
    base_size: "16px"\
    scale: "minor-third"\
  \
  spacing:\
    unit: 4\
    scale: \cf7 \strokec7 [4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64]\cf0 \strokec2 \
  \
  radius:\
    none: "0px"\
    sm: "4px"\
    md: "8px"              # Standard component rounding (cards, buttons)\
    \cf6 \strokec6 lg: "16px"\
---\
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 # LAYER 2: HUMAN & AI DESIGN RATIONALE (Markdown Prose)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 ## 1. Brand Identity & Rationale\
* \cf0 \strokec2 **The Aesthetic:** Editorial, code-inspired utility with expansive negative space.\
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 **The Goal:** The UI should feel like an intentional desktop utility tool rather than a generic SaaS template.\
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 **Layout Principle:** Rely on strict spacing grid alignments and explicit typography scales instead of heavy background colored containers.\
\
\cf6 \strokec6 ## 2. Visual Rules & Tokens Usage\
### Colors\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 * Use \cf8 \strokec8 `surface`\cf0 \strokec2  for major panel backdrops. Never inject colored gradients into containers.\
* Use \cf8 \strokec8 `primary`\cf0 \strokec2  text strictly for semantic headings (\cf8 \strokec8 `h1`\cf0 \strokec2 , \cf8 \strokec8 `h2`\cf0 \strokec2 ). \
* Use \cf8 \strokec8 `muted`\cf0 \strokec2  for secondary descriptive metadata text and light structural borders.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 ### Layout & Spacing\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 * Every padding and margin value must align to an increment of the \cf8 \strokec8 `spacing.unit`\cf0 \strokec2  (4px grid).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 Keep mobile viewports strictly linear. Do not use multi-column card splits on viewports narrower than 768px.\
\
\cf6 \strokec6 ## 3. UI Component Specifications\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 ### Buttons\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 * **Default Structure:** Flat, borders must use \cf8 \strokec8 `radius.md`\cf0 \strokec2  (8px). \
* **Interaction:** Micro-interactions only. Use \cf8 \strokec8 `transition: all 160ms ease-out`\cf0 \strokec2 . \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 **Hover State:** Shift background contrast or brightness slightly. Never scale or pop buttons dynamically.\
\
\cf6 \strokec6 ### Inputs & Cards\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 * Active text inputs must throw a \cf8 \strokec8 `1px solid`\cf0 \strokec2  border using the \cf8 \strokec8 `accent`\cf0 \strokec2  color token.\
* Cards do not use drop shadows. Separate cards using a \cf8 \strokec8 `1px`\cf0 \strokec2  crisp outline colored with the \cf8 \strokec8 `muted`\cf0 \strokec2  token.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 ## 4. Design Boundary Conditions (Dos and Don'ts)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 ### \uc0\u9989  DO\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 * Maintain generous \cf8 \strokec8 `padding`\cf0 \strokec2  inside lists and tables (minimum 16px).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 Use custom SVG icons styled entirely with monochromatic fills.\
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 Ensure all text against background variations maintains a minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio (WCAG AA compliance).\
\
\cf6 \strokec6 ### \uc0\u10060  DON'T\
* \cf0 \strokec2 **No AI Slop:** Do not generate random purple/blue gradients or generic rounded buttons unless explicitly defined.\
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 **No Inline Tooling:** Do not invent color variations outside of the defined YAML palette.\
\cf6 \strokec6 * \cf0 \strokec2 **No Complex Modals:** Avoid stackable modals; prefer contextual inline layout expansion instead.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

